      "verified_at": "2026-10-20T08:07:36.539Z",
      "notes": "Language: Chiquitano (ISO 639-3 ccb, Glottolog chiq1253), spoken in central Santa Cruz Department of eastern Bolivia and Mato Grosso, Brazil. Area confirmed by Wikipedia (Chiquitano languages) and San Ramón Municipality page (Ñuflo de Chávez, Santa Cruz; 763 Chiquitano residents per 2024 census). Seeds checked against documented Jesuit Missions of Chiquitos (Concepcion, San Javier, San Miguel de Velasco, San Ignacio de Velasco, Santa Ana de Velasco, San Rafael de Velasco, San Jose de Chiquitos, San Juan) and Santa Cruz settlements (Robore, San Matias, Puerto Suarez). San Antonio de Lomerio confirmed as a real municipality. Removed SanXavier (duplicate of SanJavier - same mission, different orthography). Removed SanRoqueDeMonte, Quijarro (province name, not a settlement), ElCarmenRiveroTorres, SanJuanDeDios, SanJuanDePozo (no primary-source evidence as settlements in the Chiquitano area). Lomerio communities (SanIsidro, SanPedro, SanPablo, SanMiguel, SanFrancisco, SanJose, SanCarlos, SanLuis, SanJoaquin, SanMartin, SanMateo, SanLucas de Lomerio) are in the documented Lomerio region with Chiquitano presence but not individually sourced to primary documents."
